meaning:
Meek flips a passage from Psalm 23:4:

Yea, though I walk through the valley of the shadow of death,
I will fear no evil;
For You are with me;
Your rod and Your staff, they comfort me

However, Mill replaces “shadow of death” with “ladder in flex” (his gun is cocked—"ladder" is Philly slang for a clip) to change the meaning of the quoted psalm and to fit with the rhyme.

Similar to Young Thug’s lines on his version of Check.



Meek Mill is getting checks from tours and endorsements. He checks himself to see if he is making the most money he can. Meek is probably getting checks from Puma, artists he cosigned and features he does. Meek is similar to Big Sean in a sense because they both share a same ideal on checks;

Check after check, checking off my check list"
